{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","title":"color"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/color"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","title":"MXLMetronome","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displayed in the music notation.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/color":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/color","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/color","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","title":"color"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"}}}